// `*b += 6` on a `let b: Box<i64>` (no `mut`): E0596, refused (it compiled and RAN — the bare `deref_mut()` receiver was never asked). ONE TOKEN from pass/bc_mutplace_box_compound. Was soundness-queue row derefmut_compound_recv_immut_admit (tier 2).
// PROBES.md 2026-09-08a: a place in a mutable-use position takes the DerefMut/IndexMut step at every level, a Deref-only/Index-only step is refused, and the bare `deref_mut()` receiver is asked the binding-mut question.
package bc_mutplace_box_compound_immut_fail;
fn main() -> i32 {
    let b: Box<i64> = Box::new(1i64);
    *b += 6i64;
    if *b != 7i64 { return 1i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
